The PS5 sysroot is FreeBSD-derived but its libc has no close_range(); Boost.Process v2 assumes
every FreeBSD does. Make that path opt-in so the portable /dev/fd fallback is used. Sunshine only
includes the v1 headers, so this merely keeps the (unused) compiled v2 library building.

--- a/libs/process/src/posix/close_handles.cpp
+++ b/libs/process/src/posix/close_handles.cpp
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 // linux has close_range since 5.19
 
 
-#if defined(__FreeBSD__)
+#if defined(__FreeBSD__) && defined(BOOST_PROCESS_V2_USE_FREEBSD_CLOSE_RANGE)
 
 // https://www.freebsd.org/cgi/man.cgi?query=close_range&apropos=0&sektion=0&manpath=FreeBSD+13.1-RELEASE+and+Ports&arch=default&format=html
 // __FreeBSD__
